\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou great mysterious God  unknown,
\par Whose love hath gently led me on,
\par Even from my infant days,
\par Mine inmost soul expose to view,
\par And tell me if I ever knew
\par Thy justifying grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. If I have only  known Thy fear.
\par And followed with a heart sincere
\par Thy drawings from above,
\par Now, now the further grace bestow,
\par And let my sprinkled conscience know
\par Thy sweet forgiving love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Short of Thy love I would not stop,
\par A stranger to the gospel hope,
\par The sense of sin forgiven;
\par I would not, Lord, my soul deceive,
\par Without the inward witness live,
\par That antepast of heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If now the witness were in me,
\par Would He not testify of Thee
\par In Jesus reconciled?
\par And should I not with faith draw nigh,
\par And boldly Abba, Father! cry,
\par And know myself Thy child?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Whate'er obstructs Thy pardoning love,
\par Or sin or righteousness, remove,
\par Thy glory to display;
\par Mine heart of unbelief convince,
\par And now absolve me from my sins,
\par And take them all away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Father, in me reveal Thy Son,
\par And to my inmost soul make known
\par How merciful Thou art:
\par The secret of Thy love reveal,
\par And by Thine hallowing Spirit dwell
\par For ever in my heart.
\par                      Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
